      "topLeftX": 400,
      "topLeftY": 791,
      "bottomRightX": 721,
      "bottomRightY": 960,
      "content": "In summary, we proposed and demonstrated 3D-DGH, in which a hologram is noniteratively and directly calculated with a deep convolutional neural network to optically reproduce a 3D target pattern in a given class. The network was trained with a loss between the target pattern and multislice propagation from the hologram synthesized by the network. The 3D-DGH method was numerically and experimentally compared with the 3D-GS method. In the demonstrations, the EMNIST database was used for the training and test data sets. U-Net was employed for the network architecture of 3D-DGH as a first trial, although U-Net was not optimized for this application.",
